  "calculationNotes": [
    "For max-content, normal collapses the two spaces to one: 20 + 10 + 20 = 50 CSS px.",
    "For max-content, pre-wrap preserves both spaces: 20 + 20 + 20 = 60 CSS px.",
    "For min-content, the two words are separate unbreakable segments of 20 CSS px; preserved pre-wrap spaces hang at the line end and do not enlarge the 20 CSS px track.",
    "The 25 CSS px soft-wrap case fits one 20 CSS px word. The preserved separator is allowed to hang; line-height 10 CSS px and two lines produce a 20 CSS px row.",
    "CSS Grid §6 says a direct text sequence containing only white space is not rendered as a grid item. Therefore the whitespace-only max-content case has zero-sized tracks and the block following a whitespace-only sequence auto-places in the first grid cell.",
    "Leading and trailing preserved spaces each contribute two Ahem advances to max-content: 20 + 20 = 40 CSS px.",
    "With the default tab size of eight spaces, the tab after XX advances from x=20 to the next 80px stop, then XX ends at x=100."
  ]
}
